# T6.1: does holding a trig in GRID RECORDING and turning a knob make a p-lock? FLTR page first
# (a sound parameter: the control, locks on stock), then the delay page: A (TIME, stock) and G
# (the delay page's 8th knob in the grown/pathc variants), then the chorus page: E (a grown row).
# Trig 1 is placed first (REC, trig 1); each lock is made on trig 1 of track 1.
wait-emu 0.5
tap 0                # RECORD: grid recording on
wait-emu 0.3
tap q                # place a trig on step 1 (if there is one already, this removes it)
wait-emu 0.3
png 00-grid
tap bracketleft      # FLTR page
wait-emu 0.5
down q
wait-emu 0.3
tap 1                # FLTR A (attack), one step
wait-emu 0.2
tap 1
wait-emu 0.3
png 01-fltr-lock-a
up q
wait-emu 0.4
down space
wait-emu 0.1
tap l                # FUNC+FX: delay page
wait-emu 0.1
up space
wait-emu 0.5
down q
wait-emu 0.3
tap 1                # TIME
wait-emu 0.2
tap 1
wait-emu 0.3
png 02-delay-lock-a
tap 7                # G
wait-emu 0.2
tap 7
wait-emu 0.3
png 03-delay-lock-g
up q
wait-emu 0.4
tap Down
wait-emu 0.3
tap Down
wait-emu 0.4
down q
wait-emu 0.3
tap 5                # chorus E
wait-emu 0.2
tap 5
wait-emu 0.3
png 04-chorus-lock-e
up q
wait-emu 0.4
tap 0                # RECORD off
wait-emu 0.4
png 05-end
